# ---- no-go theorems / walls
n('flow-blindness-sl2','obstruction','Flow-blindness no-go (SL2)','The backward flow Phi -> e^{-eps u^2} Phi preserves every flow-stable hypothesis yet has a non-real zero for every eps > 0 (Rodgers-Tao). No flow-invariant, zero-reality-sound hypothesis class containing the t = 0 profile proves RH. Obstruction map F1 / control HEAT.','proved','no','yes',PA+'flow-blindness; src/data/flow-blindness-no-go.js',['heat-flow','lambda','antibridge'])
n('ns-rigid-native-span','obstruction','THEOREM NS-RIGID (native-span softness dichotomy)','Every finite Caratheodory-Pick positivity statement P_S >= 0 on the flow native span is either flow-stable (survives past Rodgers-Tao) or already refutes RH; the only flow-critical member is the all-S family, which is RH. Matches obstruction map P3/P5 (finite Pick stages).','proved','no','yes',PA+'twin-ns-rigid; src/data/imp-95530-native-span-arithmetic-input-rigidity.js',['pick','heat-flow','weil'])
n('res-t-resolution-law','obstruction','THEOREM RES-T (fixed-support Weil positivity resolution law)','W_T >= 0 follows from verified height only for T < T_X (T_X = 3.88 at X = 3e12); beyond that its content is a pointwise short-Dirichlet-polynomial bound (pointwise Hilbert-transform wall).','proved','no','no',PA+'twin-res-t; src/data/imp-95543-last-lever-closure-consolidated.js',['weil','explicit-formula'])
n('theorem-u-sieve-universality','obstruction','Theorem U: sieve-algebra universality','Every freeze-calculus word in {Pi_p, T_p, scalars, sums, products} followed by exact transforms or isometries equals L(diag(m)c) for a unique m in the 2^25-dimensional sieve algebra over primes <= 97: configurations change what is provable, not what is true.','proved','yes','unknown',PA+'twin-theorem-u; src/data/perm-arch-sieve-universality-no-go-2026-09-22.js',['euler-product','twin-ladder','lean'])
n('akh-localized-barrier-nogo','obstruction','Localized barrier sum A_{k,h}: prime and zero sides closed','The localized barrier sum is height/width-bound and GRH-inert on the prime side and Montgomery-pair-correlation-gated on the zero side (59% of the p = 97 majorant mass at alpha > 1).','closed','yes','no',PA+'twin-akh-nogo; src/data/imp-95519-localized-barrier-sum-prime-zero-nogo.js',['lambda','pair-correlation'])
n('mv-cap-window-replacement','obstruction','MV-CAP: window-replacement counter-models (route 42)','xi_W = kappa xi Q_{W\'}/Q_W keeps the functional equation, order 1, residue 1, the zero-free region and explicit N(T) bounds while the every-window hypothesis H_desc fails (p_viol <= 3.0119 < 4.3743). Proved for zero-side and O-form premises; not established for explicit function-side L^2 mean values. Obstruction map P29.','proved','no','yes',PA+'route42-mv-cap-theorem; src/data/route-42-formal-mv-cap-2026-10-10.js',['large-sieve','explicit-formula','antibridge'])
n('mv-cap-function-side-gap','open-lemma','Function-side L^2 mean values exclude the MV-CAP counter-model','At sigma = 2 a Montgomery-Vaughan short-interval mean value (Delta about 2.2e4 against error about 10) and |zeta(1+it)| <= (3/4) log t exclude the window-replacement model at c0 = 5e5 (measured). MV-CAP is therefore not a theorem for explicit function-side L^2 premises.','measured','yes','no',PA+'route42-mv-cap-theorem',['large-sieve','euler-product'])
n('zero-density-lambda-inert','obstruction','Zero-density estimates are Lambda-inert','Zero-density bounds give a positive upper bound on the number of off-line zeros and never certify zero off-line zeros up to X, so they cannot tighten the barrier bound. Obstruction map Z17 / landscape pointwise wall.','closed','unknown','no',PA+'lambda-zero-density-inert; src/data/zero-density-lambda-inert-2026-07-09.js',['zero-free','lambda','large-sieve'])
n('lane-audit-h-desc','open-lemma','Lane audit: flow-descent hypothesis H_desc','The Polymath15 tail-lane object sits at abscissa > 1 where zero density is vacuous; mean-value inputs lose to the triangle inequality; the flow-descent rate is a pointwise von Mangoldt sum at zero-free-region strength. One conditional theorem: H_desc implies a lower Lambda.','conjectural','yes','yes',PA+'lane-audit; src/data/lane-arithmetic-input-audit-2026-09-22.js',['lambda','heat-flow','explicit-formula'])
n('route7-coupling-floor','obstruction','Route VII floor: sigma - 1/2 = (t/2) ln N coupling','The complete-row barrier program has floor U about 0.150 (t about 0.137, y = 0.165); N1*(t,y) = exp(Theta(1/t)). Going lower needs a tail mechanism that breaks the coupling sigma - 1/2 = (t/2) ln N, i.e. arithmetic input rather than compute. Obstruction map F6.','measured','no','no',PA+'route7-floor; '+FD+'t0-program-floor',['lambda','heat-flow'])
n('mollifier-length-ceiling-l1','obstruction','Mollifier-length ceiling in the l^1 certificate class','In the Wiener-algebra certificate class the infimum over all mollifiers of the lane mass is min(1, gamma ||A/B||); this caps the length lever at Lambda about 0.154-0.156 and excludes coefficient-magnitude certificates below about 0.1455 at X = 6.0e12.','measured','no','no',PA+'lambda-barrier-length-ceiling; src/data/barrier-mollifier-length-ceiling-2026-09.js',['mollifier','lambda'])
n('perm-atlas-isometric-nogain','obstruction','Permutation atlas: isometric families give no gain','All 25! prime orders, divisor / 25-defect / five-shell / Heat-Euler fibre forms and DFT / chirp / bicomplex / twistor isometries are conditioning or alternative coordinates only; budgets cannot be added.','closed','yes','unknown',PA+'twin-perm-atlas-nogain; dag:program-dag#fam-bicomplex-twistor',['twin-ladder','twistor','euler-product'])
n('five-shell-p97-identity','identity','Five-shell P97 identity','Sieving by the 25 primes <= 97 in four blocks gives five pairwise-orthogonal Fourier shells and the exact cocycle E97 = Y_4(0) - sum_g Z_g(0). Lean kernel-checked (five_shell_identity).','proved','yes','yes',PA+'twin-five-shell; src/data/imp-95003-five-shell-identity.js',['euler-product','lean','twin-ladder'])

# ---- twin ladder objects
n('twin-ladder-network','object','Twin ladder (direct + dual ladders, bridge chi)','Two-sided cascade: a direct prime-resonator ladder encoding zeta(s), a dual ladder encoding zeta(1-s), coupled by chi(s) = pi^{s-1/2} Gamma((1-s)/2)/Gamma(s/2); |chi(1/2+it)| = 1, so the bridge is lossless exactly on the critical line.','proved','yes','yes',PA+'twin-ladder-def; '+PA+'twin-bridge-chi',['twin-ladder','bridge','euler-product'])
n('shift-bridge-threshold','identity','Shift-bridge threshold theorem (a-dial)','With E_a(z) = X(a - iz) and kernel K_a, strict diagonal positivity at shift a holds exactly when a >= Delta (maximal horizontal zero displacement); K_a PSD for every a > 0 iff Delta = 0 iff RH. E_a(z) = Xi(z + ia), so T3(a) is "no zero with Re s > 1/2 + a". Obstruction map G20.','proved','no','yes',PA+'twin-shift-bridge-threshold; '+PA+'twin-t3-strip',['bridge','de-branges','zero-free'])
n('ghost-zero-witness','mechanism','Ghost-zero witness','A zero 1/2 + delta + i gamma with delta > 0 gives, for every 0 < a < delta, an interior zero of E_a at -gamma + i(delta - a), certifying failure of bridge positivity. One inverse Blaschke ghost = one rank-one negative square of the bridge kernel (Krein-Langer / Pontryagin index). Obstruction map G6/Q6.','proved','no','yes',PA+'twin-godel-witness; '+PA+'twin-blaschke-ghosts',['bridge','de-branges','pick'])
n('four-closure-routes-equivalence','obstruction','Theorem 16.1: closure routes A/B/C/D are one problem','Schur contractivity |X(w-a)/X(w+a)| < 1, de Branges positivity K_a PSD, hidden-square factorization and the Weil / twin-ladder norm square Q_TL >= 0 are equivalent (Delta = 0). Route A is circular without a zero-free region. Obstruction map P1, G2.','proved','no','yes',PA+'twin-thm-16-1; src/data/closure-routes-section.js',['de-branges','weil','pick','twin-ladder'])
n('hidden-square-conj-16-4','open-lemma','Hidden-square kernel factorization (Conj 16.4)','Find a Gram factorization of K_a built from the completed kernel Phi rather than from the zeros. Pointwise sine-cosine identities leave sign-indefinite cross terms, so any factorization must be non-local; none has been constructed. RH-equivalent.','conjectural','unknown','yes',PA+'twin-route-c-hidden-square; src/data/hidden-square-program-section.js',['de-branges','theta','bridge','spinor'])
n('cdb-exist','conjecture','CDB-Exist: Phi-built de Branges canonical system','For every a > 0 there is a de Branges canonical system built from Phi whose Cayley transform is Theta_a = E_a^#/E_a. Unifies Conjectures 16.4, 16.6, 18.1. RH-equivalent.','conjectural','unknown','yes',PA+'twin-cdb-exist; src/data/imp-1241-unified-existence-conjecture.js',['de-branges','bridge'])
n('qtl-weil-delay-form','identity','Twin-ladder Weil norm square Q_TL','Q_TL[h] = A_inf[h] - 2 sum_p sum_m (log p) p^{-m/2} Re C_h(m log p): the Weil explicit formula in log-prime delay coordinates. Under RH the zero side is a square; off-line zeros give negative-norm ghost states.','proved','yes','yes',PA+'twin-route-d-weil-norm',['weil','explicit-formula','twin-ladder'])
n('prime-delay-domination-15-4','conjecture','Conj 15.4: Re xi\'/xi > 0 on sigma > 1/2','Infinitesimal shift contractivity: the completed rightward drift of xi dominates the prime-delay echo train right of the line. Re xi\'/xi(s) > 0 on Re s > 1/2 is RH-equivalent (Lagarias 1999). Obstruction map P8 / G8.','conjectural','yes','yes',PA+'twin-conj-15-4',['bridge','shear','pick'])
n('volterra-not-reduction','obstruction','Volterra norm bound is not a reduction','At the Riemann Phi, I - VV* crosses zero under scaling while K_a stays PSD: no scalar normalization equates the scale-bounded sublevel set with the scale-invariant cone. Rigorous ||V|| <= sqrt(I0 J_a) about 2.94e-4 bounds an RH-equivalent object. Obstruction map P20.','closed','no','yes',PA+'twin-volterra-not-reduction; '+ID+'hs-bound-IJ',['de-branges','twin-ladder'])
n('ka-offdiagonal-hankel-g7','open-lemma','G7: off-diagonal endpoint-Hankel positivity of R','The scalar mu-pass cover pins every diagonal of R = G_pass^{-1/2} G_shear G_pass^{-1/2} strictly below 1 (residual deficit 0); G_shear is an off-diagonal endpoint-Hankel form, and ||R|| <= 1 (K_a >= 0) is the untouched RH-equivalent operator step.','conjectural','unknown','yes',LR+'G7; '+PA+'twin-mupass-rh',['shear','de-branges','bridge'])
n('frozen-rung-pt-equivalence','identity','Frozen-rung <=> Platt-Trudgian','Freezing twin-ladder rungs is the verified-height certificate in operator form: by Sylvester inertia frozen-rung certificates cannot beat verified height, and PT is the winding form of the frozen-rung index certificate. Converse conditional on (ZR).','proved','no','no',PA+'frozen-rung-pt; src/data/frozen-rung-pt-equivalence-2026-07-31.js',['twin-ladder','lean','zero-channel'])
n('zr-zero-repulsion','open-lemma','(ZR) zero-repulsion hypothesis','Single named hypothesis in the kernel-verified L2 detection-modulus theorem (Aristotle wave 5, no nonstandard axioms). Discharging it promotes frozen-rung <=> Platt-Trudgian to a full theorem; it promotes a theorem, not a Lambda value.','conjectural','unknown','unknown',FD+'zr-hypothesis; formalization/lean-aristotle/frozen-rung/',['lean','twin-ladder','pair-correlation'])
n('conj-22-1-frozen-ladder','conjecture','Conjecture 22.1 and the frozen-ladder obstruction','A frozen-ladder approximation with smaller certified remainder than a baseline at equal runtime. Fourier closure + Polya-Szego zero bound + sign transfer give D >= M + 1: a Gaussian-mixture frozen ladder tracking sign changes to 3e12 needs >= 1.2363e13 coefficients. Obstruction map P30.','closed','no','no',PA+'twin-conj-22-1; '+PA+'conj22-1-obstruction',['twin-ladder','theta'])
n('levinson-in-ladder-language','mechanism','Levinson method as direct/dual weight balance','Z = 2 Re[e^{i theta}(zeta + zeta\'/(2 theta\'))]; Q(x) + Q(1-x) = const is the direct/dual weight balance. Primorial Euler-product mollifiers score below the length-truncated Mobius reference in a fixed-Q main-term proxy (theta = 1/2, T = 1e6: 0.262 vs 0.453).','measured','yes','no',PA+'dag3-levinson-bridge',['mollifier','twin-ladder','bridge'])
n('euler-product-mollifier-nogo','obstruction','Euler-product mollifiers do not reach the Mobius reference','At equal length T^{1/2} no tested Euler-product replacement (range-truncated, Radziwill-Soundararajan blocks, truncated-exp, primorial, GHK hybrid) reaches the Conrey/Levinson reference 0.4876 / 0.4530 / 0.4178 / 0.3972 at T = 1e4 / 1e6 / 1e10 / 1e16 (main-term proxy). Obstruction map P26.','measured','yes','no',PA+'ns3-euler-mollifier-no-go',['mollifier','euler-product'])
n('kappa-theta-beyond-4-7','measured-phenomenon','Conditional kappa(theta) beyond 4/7','One-piece Conrey (P deg 6, Q deg 7), conditional on the twisted second moment: kappa = 0.4249 (theta 0.6), 0.4753 (0.7), 0.5884 (1.0), 0.7703 (2.0); passes 1/2 at theta = 0.755; d kappa/d theta = 0.571 at 4/7. Barrier: Kloosterman input behind 4/7.','conjectural','yes','no',PA+'route17-mollifiers-beyond-four-sevenths',['mollifier','large-sieve'])
n('alpoge-furman-inertia-mechanism','mechanism','Alpoge-Furman: Gabor compression + rank-trace + Sylvester inertia','Gabor compression of the Weil form (support [-L/2, L/2], dimension about N(T,2T)) + Montgomery second moment + rank-trace lemma + inertia gives certificate 0.5775 -> 2/3 like 1/L; R = 1.3274992963. Uses a prime-side second moment over a height-localised family with signature counting, outside the NS-RIGID span. Obstruction map P27.','measured','yes','no',PA+'route16-alpoge-furman-reproduction; '+LD+'alpoge-furman-2026',['weil','pair-correlation','explicit-formula'])

# ---- Route I / Weil
n('semilocal-sonine-trace-identity','identity','Semilocal S = {inf,2} Sonine trace identity','Tr(theta(f) P P^_S P) = W_inf(f) + W_2(f) + D_S(f), F_S = I o (u_inf u_2) (Tate factor), trace side positive (multiplier min 0.0650). The remainder D_S (log spikes at 2^k) carries 96.7% (a = 0.5) / 99.71% (a = (ln 3)/2) of the trace on the pole-free minimizer.','measured','yes','no',PA+'routes-i-semilocal-sonine-identity; src/data/rh-route-i-semilocal-sonine-trace-identity-2026-09-23.js',['weil','trace-formula','explicit-formula'])
n('ds-le-ls-pencil','measured-phenomenon','D_S <= L_S pencil and the 1.1316 crossing','Weil positivity on g-support < ln 3 is equivalent to D_S <= L_S (two RH-free functionals). Pencil D_S c = mu L_S c: mu_max < 1 on 2a <= ln 3 (margin 2.84e-3), crosses 1 at 2a* = ln 3 + 0.033 = 1.1316 through an odd vector; negativity sits in the first p = 2 resonance window (8.145, 9.875).','certified','yes','no',PA+'routes-i-ds-le-ls; '+PA+'routes-i-pencil-highres-map',['weil','trace-formula'])
n('sonine-excess-half-cusp','obstruction','Sonine-excess port obstructed past ln 2','The Connes-Consani refinement W = S - E ports to S = {inf,2} exactly (lambda_S(0) = 0.9999731), but the excess inherits exactly half the rho = 2 log cusp, so E_S o Q is unbounded above along p = 2 resonances for every 2a > ln 2; no finite-rank fix; one-prime reach a_2 = 0.565920.','closed','yes','no',PA+'routes-i-sonine-excess-port',['weil','trace-formula'])
n('s23-dirichlet-rank-obstruction','obstruction','S containing {2,3}: Dirichlet-rank obstruction','For S containing {2,3} the positive trace exists abstractly but its remainder is not a regular function: rank(Z_S^*) > 1 makes log(Z_S^*) dense in R. The remainder share does not fall as primes are added (99.71% at ln 3 to 99.99997% at ln 4 for S2, S23, S235).','closed','yes','no',PA+'routes-i-s23-multiplier-obstruction; '+PA+'route12-s23-semilocal-identity',['weil','trace-formula','euler-product'])
n('corr23-mixed-prolate-ladder','open-lemma','Mixed 2^a 3^b prolate ladder: rho-free spectral gap','The cubic tail sum |lambda|^3 = 1.769529 of the mixed {inf,2,3} ladder has a rho-free geometric majorant; termwise-uniform continuity fails by S-unit density. corr23 continuity is conditional on sup |lambda_n| < 1 (a spectral gap not depending on zeros).','conjectural','yes','unknown',PA+'routes-i-corr23-mixed-ladder; src/data/imp-96143-route-i-mixed-ladder-23-prolate-spectrum-summability.js',['weil','trace-formula','euler-product'])
n('toeplitz-krein-sigma2','identity','Pole-free Weil positivity = T_a[sigma_2] >= 0','Pole-free Weil positivity is exactly the Toeplitz statement T_a[sigma_2] >= 0 with sigma_2 = (t^2 + 1/4)^2 w_1. Interval-certified for 2a <= 0.96; ARB-LEGE: W(h) >= 8.2045e-4 ||h||^2 for every pole-free h in L^2(-a,a), all 2a <= ln 3; lambda_1(T_a[sigma_2]) >= 0.0583.','certified','yes','no',PA+'routes-i-toeplitz-krein-cert; '+PA+'routes-i-arb-lege-cert',['weil','pick'])
n('multi-rung-arb-lege','measured-phenomenon','Multi-rung pole-free positivity margin law','Symbol w_K = 2 theta\' - sum_{n<=K} 2 Lambda(n) n^{-1/2} cos(t ln n). W >= c ||h||^2 with c = 8.55e-8 (ln 4), 2.25e-12 (ln 5), 6.25e-17 (ln 6), 5.62e-42 (ln 11, conditional); log10 c about -4.82 e^{2a} + 12.1. Obstruction map P19 / S7 (verified-height content).','certified','yes','no',PA+'route11-multi-prime-arb-lege',['weil','explicit-formula'])
n('polefree-to-weil-three-axes','obstruction','Pole-free certificate to full Weil positivity: three axes','The gap from T_a[sigma_2] >= 0 to full Weil positivity has three independent axes: reach (LP conditioning wall), pole term (Sonine bridge obstructed at ln 2), criterion completeness (per-support slice to full cone, which carries flow-blindness).','closed','unknown','no',PA+'routes-polefree-to-weil-axes',['weil'])
n('nonlocal-pole-term-bridge','open-lemma','Nonlocal / arithmetic pole-term bridge past ln 2','No local, finite-rank or fixed-measure pole-term bridge carries pole-free positivity to the full Weil form past 2a = ln 2. Nonlocal or arithmetic bridges are not excluded; soft nonlocal ones fall under flow-blindness.','conjectural','unknown','unknown',PA+'routes-nonsonine-pole-bridge; src/data/imp-97076-nonsonine-pole-term-bridge-assessment.js',['weil','trace-formula'])
n('scaling-site-arch-p2-cancellation','measured-phenomenon','Archimedean vs p = 2 cancellation across ln 2','Archimedean-only positivity radius a* = 0.3716 (odd) / 0.4101 (even) vs (ln 2)/2 = 0.3466. Positivity across ln 2 is a cancellation to 5-6 relative digits: residual/P_2 = 7.5e-5 at a = 0.5, 3.2e-6 at (ln 3)/2. The second adelic direction is block-diagonal over 2-power characters.','measured','yes','no',PA+'routes-h-scaling-site; '+PA+'routes-h-arch-p2-cancellation',['weil','trace-formula'])
n('krein-csharp-floor','open-lemma','Krein c# = lambda_min(P_a M_{sigma_2} P_a) lower bound at 2a = ln 3','Temple, Kato-Temple, Beurling-Selberg / prolate concentration, reproducing kernel, bathtub, Lehmann-Maehly all fail to certify c# > 0: best rigorous floor -3065.435, measured upper bracket +0.581059. sigma_2 is sign-indefinite, so it is not a de Branges weight.','measured','no','no',PA+'routes-krein-csharp-cohort; '+PA+'routes-krein-de-branges-gap',['weil','de-branges'])
n('dh-euler-blindness-radius','control','DH-BLIND: Weil-form Euler-blindness radius (conductor 5)','The Davenport-Heilbronn twin has Weil form >= 0.2080723937 ||h||^2 at 2a <= ln 3 and positive definite through 2a <= ln 11 (6.93e-9), finite-basis positive to a about 1.70, certified negative at a = 1.72 via the zero 0.8085 + 85.699i. Shared object: the gamma factor. Control DH.','certified','no','no',PA+'twin-dh-euler-blindness; '+PA+'dag3-dhblind-arb-ln11',['weil','antibridge'])
n('euler-detection-depth-law','measured-phenomenon','Euler-detection depth of 440 DH-type twins','Twins F_theta = sum Re(e^{i theta} chi(n)) n^{-s}, q = 5..49: 387 certified onsets a* in 0.36..3.40; Euler arms never negative. Fit a* about -0.748 + 0.387 log gamma - 0.278 log(beta - 1/2) + 0.278 log q (rms 0.139): onset follows the first off-line zero and root-number phase.','measured','no','no',PA+'route44-euler-detection-depth',['weil','hecke'])
n('epstein-euler-blindness','control','Epstein twins: Euler-blindness radius','27 Epstein zeta functions (12 discriminants, h = 2-4): certified negative witnesses; principal forms a* about log(|D|/4) - 0.13 (1.28-2.60); (2,2,3) has a* <= 0.417 < (ln 3)/2; the lowest off-line zero carries the negativity; D = -23 fails first in the odd sector.','certified','no','no',PA+'route15-epstein-euler-blindness',['weil','theta','torus'])
n('rung-toeplitz-euler-detector','mechanism','Rung Toeplitz tests detect DH at ln 2 / ln 4 / ln 6','F_DH = (Euler product over p = +-1 mod 5) x G; c(n) = 0 on non-prime-powers with a +-1 factor. Local degree-1 Toeplitz witness 2 + 2 m_2(2) = -2(1 + kappa^2) = -2.1614 at ln 2, below the Weil onset 3.44. A multiplicativity test with no RH content. Obstruction map L1.','certified','yes','yes',PA+'route30-euler-detector',['euler-product','hecke','pick'])
n('mollified-weil-reduction','identity','Mollified Weil form = plain Weil form at larger support','sum_rho h^(gamma) M(rho) M(1-rho) = W(G * G~), G = mu * g in L^2(-A, A), A = a + (1/2) log N, with g -> mu * g injective; so a*_mol >= a*_plain - (1/2) log N. Mollification merges into Route I and inherits Euler-blindness.','proved','yes','no',PA+'route19-mollified-weil-forms',['weil','mollifier'])
n('family-weil-positivity','obstruction','Family-averaged Weil positivity is Euler-blind','Averaging over the q - 2 nonprincipal characters leaves only n = 1 mod q at full weight: W_F >= 2.336 ||h||^2 at 2a = 10 (q = 257). A hybrid of 254 characters with F_DH is certified >= 0.8578 at 2a = 7.764: a positive average does not imply positive members. Obstruction map P23.','certified','yes','no',PA+'route14-family-weil-positivity',['weil','hecke'])
n('lacunary-cone-positivity','measured-phenomenon','Weil positivity on lacunary cones','Lacunary W(Lambda) <=> indeterminate Caratheodory/Stieltjes interpolation of xi\'/xi on a Blaschke node set. {4^k}: normalised Pick operator >= 3.6346e-4 (Arb); survives backward flow to eps_0 about 364. Non-separated sets near the Muntz threshold (k^p, p <~ 1.13) open at heuristic level. Obstruction map P18.','certified','no','no',PA+'route13-lacunary-cones',['pick','weil'])
n('gl2-twin-ladder','control','GL(2) twin ladder: Ramanujan per rung, not for the ladder','11a: W >= 3.2528e-8 ||h||^2 at 2a <= log 16; Delta: 6.8856e-11 at log 7. The no-Euler-product twin Delta E4^3 (off-line zeros delta = 0.186 at gamma = 52.3) is certified positive to log 7. Rung unitarity = Hasse / Deligne; this does not give GRH for the ladder.','certified','yes','no',PA+'route26-gl2-twin-ladder',['hecke','weil','twin-ladder'])

# ---- function field / geometric
n('function-field-twin-ladder','identity','Function-field twin ladder: Weil form = -(intersection form)','For curves over F_q: R_a is a degree-2g Blaschke product, T_N has exactly nu negative eigenvalues, and q^j + q^k - Gamma_j.Gamma_k = -P_j.P_k = q^{(j+k)/2} S_{k-j}; Hodge index on span{P_j} gives Q_TL >= 0 and curve RH. Obstruction map T3.','proved','yes','yes',PA+'route27-function-field-ladder; formalization/paper/function-field-twin-ladder.md',['function-field','hodge','twin-ladder','weil'])
n('ff-euler-product-fakes','control','Function-field fakes: FE + Euler product without RH','Ladder data alone do not imply RH over F_q: 215 exact functional-equation Euler-product fakes in the census boxes (17 at q = 3, 198 at q = 5; g = 2). The lift to Q stops at the missing Spec Z x Spec Z with Hodge index (O3) and the infinite zero count (O1).','proved','yes','yes',PA+'route27-function-field-ladder',['function-field','hodge','euler-product'])
