n('mirror-euler-rate-t0','mechanism','t = 0 Euler-product descent rate for a topmost zero','For a globally topmost zero dy/dt is bounded by a wide-Poisson term (eta >= sqrt(5) y); at t = 0 the Euler product gives a descent rate for a hypothetical topmost zero at one instant only. Extending to t > 0 needs pointwise input at sigma < 1 (NS-RIGID wall).','proved','yes','yes',PA+'twin-mirror-poisson-domination; '+PA+'twin-imp97053',['heat-flow','euler-product','zero-channel'])
